# A hash table is a data structure that maps keys to values
# using a hash function that computes an index from the key
# and places the entry in a bucket/array of entries.
# The average time complexity for lookups, insertions, and
# deletions is O(1) when the hash function distributes keys
# uniformly across buckets. In the worst case, collisions
# can degrade performance to O(n), but this is mitigated
# through collision resolution techniques like chaining
# (linked lists in buckets) or open addressing (probing
# for the next free slot). Hash tables
